        <span class="text-orange-300">"snippet":</span> <span class="text-green-400">"Wireless headphones use Bluetooth technology—short-range radio waves—to receive audio signals from devices like smartphones or computers, eliminating the need for cables. They work by pairing, converting digital audio into radio signals, and using internal components (DACs and amplifiers) to turn those signals into sound."</span>,
